From e20f126470d629cd85f9399448e0fdc0c439f9c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:28:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Event locations: free / no-payment ordering (corporate hire)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A store can be marked Event (or any store toggled 'Free'): orders are billed $0
and go straight to the kitchen with no card step — for corporate-hire events
where coffees are complimentary.

- locations.js: a per-store 'free' flag (defaults on for type=event, overridable);
  isFree() + exposed in publicList. Server-authoritative.
- orders.createOrder gains 'free' → treated as a 100% comp ($0), surcharges
  skipped, routed to the kitchen via the existing $0-order completion path.
  /api/orders and /api/pos/order set free from the LOCATION, never the client.
- Checkout: for a free store it skips the Square SDK/card entirely, hides the
  payment section + wallet buttons, shows 'No payment needed — complimentary',
  and the CTA becomes 'Place order' (the existing $0 path completes it).
- Admin Locations: 'Event (corporate hire)' store type + a 'Free / complimentary
  ordering' toggle.

Verified: isFree resolution (event/override), event checkout renders the free
flow (no card, 'Place order'), build + server checks pass.
---
